### Phase 2: Run Reviews (Parallel)

**Produces:** REVIEW_FOCUS_OUTPUTS
<!-- curation:on -->
**Requires:** DIFF_RANGE, REVIEW_DIR, TIMESTAMP, DECISIONS_CONTEXT, FEATURE_KNOWLEDGE, PR_DESCRIPTION, PRIOR_RESOLUTIONS, REVIEW_FOCUS_LIST, DIFF_CLASS, DIFF_FILES
<!-- curation:off -->
**Requires:** DIFF_RANGE, REVIEW_DIR, TIMESTAMP, FEATURE_KNOWLEDGE, PR_DESCRIPTION, PRIOR_RESOLUTIONS, REVIEW_FOCUS_LIST, DIFF_CLASS, DIFF_FILES
<!-- curation:end -->

Spawn Review agents **in a single message**, one per focus in REVIEW_FOCUS_LIST (max 20 per worktree):

- `code`: the 8 core reviews on the full `diff.patch` (lean keeps 3), plus the language and conditional focuses Phase 1 added.
- `docs-only`, `tests-only`, `lockfile-only`: only the reduced set Phase 1 names, each reading `diff.patch`; a mixed non-code diff runs the union. No language or conditional focus is spawned, whatever its trigger.

| Focus | Runs | Pattern Skill | DIFF_FILE |
|-------|------|---------------|-----------|
| security | ✓ | devflow:security | diff.patch |
| architecture | ✓ | devflow:architecture | diff.patch |
| performance | ✓ | devflow:performance | diff.patch |
| complexity | ✓ | devflow:complexity | diff.patch |
| consistency | ✓ | devflow:consistency | diff.patch |
| regression | ✓ | devflow:regression | diff.patch |
| testing | ✓ | devflow:testing | diff.patch |
| reliability | ✓ | devflow:reliability | diff.patch |
| typescript | stamp-gated | devflow:typescript | diff-typescript.patch |
| react | stamp-gated | devflow:react | diff-react.patch |
| accessibility | stamp-gated | devflow:accessibility | diff-accessibility.patch |
| ui-design | stamp-gated | devflow:ui-design | diff-ui-design.patch |
| go | stamp-gated | devflow:go | diff-go.patch |
| java | stamp-gated | devflow:java | diff-java.patch |
| python | stamp-gated | devflow:python | diff-python.patch |
| rust | stamp-gated | devflow:rust | diff-rust.patch |
| database | conditional | devflow:database | diff.patch |
| dependencies | conditional | devflow:dependencies | diff.patch |
| documentation | conditional | devflow:documentation | diff.patch |
| compliance | diff-driven | devflow:compliance | diff.patch |

Review agent count: `code` runs 8 core +1-12 at `full`, up to 2 fewer at `standard`, 3-4 at lean; a reduced class or a mix runs 2-6.

{{compliance_focus_inject()}}

Each Review agent invocation (all in one message, **NOT background**):
```
Agent(subagent_type="Review", run_in_background=false):
"Review focusing on {focus}. Load the pattern skill via the Skill tool: Skill(skill="devflow:{focus}").
Follow 6-step process from devflow:review-methodology.
PR: #{pr_number}, Base: {base_branch}
WORKTREE_PATH: {worktree_path}  (omit if cwd)
DIFF_FILE: {diff_file}  (absolute: {REVIEW_DIR}/diff.patch, or {REVIEW_DIR}/diff-{focus}.patch for a language focus, per the table)
DIFF_RANGE: {DIFF_RANGE}  (information only)
<!-- curation:on -->
DECISIONS_CONTEXT: {decisions_context}
<!-- curation:end -->
FEATURE_KNOWLEDGE: {feature_knowledge}
PR_DESCRIPTION: <pr-description>{pr_description}</pr-description>
PRIOR_RESOLUTIONS: <prior-resolution-summary>{prior_resolutions}</prior-resolution-summary>
{COMPLIANCE_FOCUS_DIRECTIVE}  (compliance focus only)
If PRIOR_RESOLUTIONS is not (none), follow Cross-Cycle Awareness in review.md.
<!-- curation:on -->
Follow devflow:apply-decisions to scan the index and Read full ADR/PF bodies on demand.
<!-- curation:end -->
Follow devflow:apply-feature-knowledge for FEATURE_KNOWLEDGE — feature-specific patterns and anti-patterns inform findings.
IMPORTANT: Write report to {worktree_path}/.devflow/docs/reviews/{branch-slug}/{timestamp}/{focus}.md using Write tool"
```

In multi-worktree mode, process worktrees **sequentially**: Phases 1-4 for one worktree, then the next.

### Phase 3: Synthesis → Review Comment (Sequential)

**Produces:** REVIEW_SUMMARY, PR_COMMENT
**Requires:** REVIEW_FOCUS_OUTPUTS, REVIEW_DIR, PR_INFO, GATE_LEVEL, REVIEW_FOCUS_LIST

**WAIT** for Phase 2. For each worktree, run steps 3a and 3b in sequence:

**Step 3a — Synthesize agent** per worktree:
```
Agent(subagent_type="Synthesize", run_in_background=false):
"Mode: review
WORKTREE_PATH: {worktree_path}  (omit if cwd)
REVIEW_BASE_DIR: {worktree_path}/.devflow/docs/reviews/{branch-slug}/{timestamp}
TIMESTAMP: {timestamp}
CYCLE_NUMBER: {cycle_number}
GATE_LEVEL: {GATE_LEVEL}
FOCUSES: {REVIEW_FOCUS_LIST}
PRIOR_RESOLUTIONS: <prior-resolution-summary>{prior_resolutions}</prior-resolution-summary>
Include Convergence Status section in review-summary.md.
Aggregate findings, determine merge recommendation.
Output: {worktree_path}/.devflow/docs/reviews/{branch-slug}/{timestamp}/review-summary.md"
```

**Step 3b — Git agent (post-review-summary)** per worktree (after Step 3a writes review-summary.md):
```
Agent(subagent_type="Git", run_in_background=false):
"OPERATION: post-review-summary
PR_NUMBER: {pr_number}
REVIEW_SUMMARY_PATH: .devflow/docs/reviews/{branch-slug}/{timestamp}/review-summary.md
CYCLE_NUMBER: {cycle_number}
REVIEW_TIMESTAMP: {timestamp}
REVIEW_PUBLICATION: {REVIEW_PUBLICATION}
WORKTREE_PATH: {worktree_path}  (omit if cwd)
Posts the consolidated review-summary comment (marker-deduped by the operation on the cycle+timestamp pair)."
```

### Phase 4: Write Review Head Marker & Report

**Requires:** BRANCH_INFO, REVIEW_DIR

Per worktree, after successful completion:
1. In one Bash call run `M="$(git -C "{worktree_path}" rev-parse --absolute-git-dir)/devflow/reviews/{branch-slug}" && mkdir -p "$M" && git -C "{worktree_path}" rev-parse HEAD > "$M/.last-review-head"`. A failed or refused write never stops the run and is not retried another way.
2. Display results from all agents:
   - Merge recommendation (from Synthesize agent)
   - Issue counts by category (🔴 blocking / ⚠️ should-fix / ℹ️ pre-existing)
   - Review comment status: POSTED / POSTED+TRUNCATED (body exceeded 60k after redaction) / SKIPPED (D7 dedup) / DEGRADED (from Git)
   - Publication status: FULL (private repo) | FULL (config override) | STUB (public repository) | OFF (publication disabled by config) | STUB (visibility undeterminable) | STUB (evidence policy) (from Git agent)
   - Any base `TRACEABILITY: DEGRADED` line from Step 0c, as returned
   - Artifact paths

## Architecture

```
/code-review
│
├─ Phase 0: Worktree Discovery & Pre-flight, Steps 0a-0f (Git agent per worktree, parallel)
│  ├─ Step 0b: Resolve the compliance lens and gate level
│
├─ Per worktree (SEQUENTIAL):
│  │
│  ├─ Phase 1: Analyze changed files
│  │  ├─ Classify the diff (paths.txt → DIFF_CLASS)
│  │  ├─ Choose the focuses
│  │  └─ Write diff.patch and diff-{focus}.patch
│  │
│  ├─ Phase 2: Reviews (PARALLEL within worktree), one per REVIEW_FOCUS_LIST focus
│  │  ├─ code: core (diff.patch), language (diff-{focus}.patch), conditional
│  │  └─ docs-only / tests-only / lockfile-only: the reduced set (diff.patch)
│  │
│  ├─ Phase 3: Synthesis → Review Comment (SEQUENTIAL within worktree)
│  │  ├─ Step 3a: Synthesize agent (mode: review, writes review-summary.md)
│  │  └─ Step 3b: Git agent (post-review-summary)
│  │
│  └─ Phase 4: Write .last-review-head + display results
```

## Edge Cases

| Case | Handling |
|------|----------|
| `--full` in multi-worktree mode | Applies to all worktrees (global modifier). It sets the diff range, never the gate level |
| Review comment already posted | Git agent matches its own marker on the `{cycle, timestamp}` pair → skip silently (D7); a re-review in the same cycle (different timestamp) posts its own comment. The marker's format belongs to the operation |
| Docs-only diff | Its Step 1.1 set, narrowed by level |
| Tests-only diff | Its Step 1.1 set, narrowed by level |
| Lockfile-only diff | Its Step 1.1 set, narrowed by level |
| Mixed non-code diff | The union of the matching sets |
| A path matching no class pattern, or an empty path list | `code` (fail-safe) |
| A file moved across classes | `--no-renames` lists both paths, so a code path makes the diff `code` |
| Path listing above about 40 lines | Read in ranges (Step 1.1) |
| Language files changed, plugin not installed | The focus is absent from the stamped line: not spawned |
| `reviewPublication: off` | Git agent skips posting the review comment (OFF) — except that, only when `EVIDENCE_POLICY` is `required`, Step 0f passes `stub` and a counts-only STUB comment posts |

## Backwards Compatibility

- **Gate level**: `full` runs the sets named here; the default `standard` and `lean` narrow them. `devflow gates --set full` keeps them.

## Principles

1. **Orchestration only** - Command spawns agents, doesn't do git/review work itself. The exceptions are the read-only Phase 0 probes (`git worktree list`, `git -C ... branch --show-current`, `git -C ... cat-file -t`, `git -C ... rev-parse`), the bounded Phase 1 path listing and the redirect-only writes (`diff.patch`, `diff-{focus}.patch`, the marker). Redirect-only writes print nothing
2. **Parallel, not background** - Multiple agents in one message, but `run_in_background=false` so phases complete before proceeding
3. **Git agent for git work** - All git operations go through Git agent, except the exceptions named in Principle 1; redirect-only writes print nothing
4. **Honest reporting** - Display agent outputs directly
5. **Incremental by default** - Only review new changes unless `--full` specified
